# Gemini Notebook (NotebookLM) Source Notes

## Source refresh behavior
Web page sources (e.g. /corpus) are static snapshots taken at import time.
No auto-refresh — unlike Google Docs/Sheets/Slides, which Google added
auto-sync for in May 2026. Any edit to the live page after it's added as
a source requires manually opening the source and re-syncing, or removing
and re-adding it. No notification when a source goes stale.

## Practice going forward
- Do corpus content edits in batches, not continuously.
- Re-sync /corpus in NotebookLM immediately after any edit.
- Prefer editing during low-traffic hours (late night IST lines up with
  low US/EU traffic).
- Refresh itself takes seconds to low minutes to reflect — the real risk
  is forgetting to trigger it at all, not the refresh window itself.

## Favicon cache-bust
Source list can show a stale/wrong favicon — this is Google's crawler
caching the icon keyed to the exact URL, not to the "add source" action.
Fix: append an unused query string to force a fresh crawl, e.g.
https://synergetics.pages.dev/corpus?v=2 — confirmed working.
Quartz ignores unknown query params, so the real page is unaffected.

Current value in use: v=2
Next time it's needed: bump to v=3 (never reuse or randomize — keeps it
unambiguous which cache-bust has already been tried).

## Known cosmetic non-issue
White background tile behind source icons in NotebookLM's source menu is
NotebookLM's own UI chrome, not fixable from the site side. Not pursued.

